JD_server.py,JD_server.py,dac433bb43ad99cc866290e8085efa9b5f4568be,Amit-Shriram/Open-voice,https://api.github.com/repositories/836199886/contents/JD_server.py?ref=624673f5efb9ec0d81203a768b293682e8788d85,https://api.github.com/repositories/836199886/git/blobs/dac433bb43ad99cc866290e8085efa9b5f4568be,https://github.com/Amit-Shriram/Open-voice/blob/624673f5efb9ec0d81203a768b293682e8788d85/JD_server.py,,,0,0,0,38,2024-09-27T14:11:11Z,0,0,"# Introduction  
Huhoka Recruitment Bot is a project to automate interview processes.
It involves: 
- Parsing a resume: Using pypdf to read the pdf
- LangGraph: Using the llama-v3 open source model on HuggingFace
- Text-to-speech: Using OpenVoice (can give desired voice of the audio)
- Created as an API: (using FastAPI)
- Currently streamlit is the frontend 

# Getting Started
1.	Installation process

    Clone the repo:
    ```sh
    git clone https://github.com/your_username_/Project-Name.git
    ```
    Install the required libraries:
    ```sh
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    ```
    

2.	Software dependencies

    Text-to-speech implemented with OpenVoice. Requires the client.py file to be in the same directory as the downloaded OpenVoice folder for the model.

3.	API references
    Get a free API Key at https://huggingface.co/.
    Create a .env file 
    ```txt
    HUGGINGFACEHUB_API_TOKEN = ""your_token""
    ```
    The hugging face repo id being used: *meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct*


# Build and Test
In one terminal:
```sh
cd fastapi 
streamlit run client.py 
```
In another terminal:
```sh
cd fastapi 
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Upload a resume pdf. 
The recruitment bot will ask a question to the candidate based on their resume (audio and text generated). 
Type in the answer. 
A follow-up question will be asked. 
Continue till the interview is over. 
Total number of questions asked can be set in the fastapi/client.py file (currently set to 2).

The LangGraph workflow is as follows:

![alt text](img/LangGraphWorkflow.jpg)

# Roadmap 
1. Using websockets with whisper model for real time transcription. Integrate real-time speech-to-text functionality: Using the fasterwhisper model
2. Using LangSmith to evaluate the interview? Or an LLM."
