## Remove old venv and create a new one
```
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .\venv
py -3.11 -m venv venv

.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1


python -m pip install --upgrade pip


```

## go to venv

```
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

pip install -r ""requirements_win.txt""
```

## Start the frontend

```
Option 1: Python Data Processing Frontend (Recommended)
This uses pandas to process data files like CSV, SAS7BDAT, etc.:

streamlit run frontend_python.py

Option 2: SQL Database Management Frontend
This uses SQL to manage database files (.db) or remote SQL servers:

streamlit run frontend_sql3.py

Option 3: Backend-only Processing
For pure backend processing without UI:

python backend_db_conn.py
# or
python backend_db_up.py

```

## Database Requirements: Optional but Supported

This project is flexible and doesn't strictly require a database to run, but it supports multiple data sources:
1. No Database Required - frontend_python.py
Works with file-based data: CSV, RDS, SAS7BDAT files
Uses pandas to process data directly from files
You can start this immediately with the sample data files in the data/ folder
2. Optional Database Support - frontend_sql3.py
Supports SQLite databases (like the included Chinook.db)
Supports SQL Server connections (for clinical trial data)
Can work with uploaded .db files or remote database connections
3. Available Sample Data
The data/ folder contains:
CSV files: passenger_info.csv, passenger_fare.csv
RDS files: adsl.rds, adlb.rds, adae.rds
SAS7BDAT files: adsl.sas7bdat, adae.sas7bdat, advs.sas7bdat
SQLite database: Chinook.db"
