ai_manager.py,ai_manager.py,bc45cd544cf5d25dde7ea44d943a908c6ca6c627,SSchryba/BRO_AI_Beta3.0,https://api.github.com/repositories/1011972513/contents/ai_manager.py?ref=1fcdbffececde49b5c8cab74445355482346959f,https://api.github.com/repositories/1011972513/git/blobs/bc45cd544cf5d25dde7ea44d943a908c6ca6c627,https://github.com/SSchryba/BRO_AI_Beta3.0/blob/1fcdbffececde49b5c8cab74445355482346959f/ai_manager.py,,,0,0,0,1,2025-07-01T15:58:52Z,0,0,"# 🧱 Bro_AI - Your Digital Construction Buddy

An autonomous AI agent for Raspberry Pi 4 with a distinctive New England construction worker personality. Bro_AI features **performance-optimized operation**, graceful fallbacks, modular architecture, facial recognition, voice interaction, and a beautiful touchscreen interface.

![Bro_AI Demo](https://via.placeholder.com/800x400/ff6b35/ffffff?text=Bro_AI+Construction+Buddy)

## 🚧 New Features & Optimizations

### ⚡ Performance & Reliability
- **Optimized for Pi 4**: Custom performance tuning and resource management
- **Graceful Fallbacks**: Works even with missing optional dependencies
- **Smart Dependency Detection**: Automatically adapts to available hardware
- **Multiple Installation Modes**: Minimal, Basic, Advanced, Full
- **Robust Error Handling**: Continues operation despite component failures
- **Memory Management**: Intelligent caching and lazy loading

### 🎛️ Multiple Operation Modes
- **Web Mode**: Full web interface with touchscreen support
- **Console Mode**: Command-line only operation
- **Test Mode**: Comprehensive system testing and validation
- **Kiosk Mode**: Auto-start optimized for dedicated displays

### 🔧 Modular Architecture
- **Core System**: Centralized brain with configuration management
- **Feature Modules**: Pluggable components for voice, vision, AI, security
- **Interface Layers**: Separate voice and web UI handling
- **USB Hardware Support**: Enhanced USB device management

## 🎭 Core Features

### 🎯 Personality & Interaction
- **Distinctive Voice**: New England construction worker personality with blue-collar attitude
- **Animated Interface**: Floating emoji face with expressions and animations
- **Voice Control**: Full speech-to-text and text-to-speech capabilities with fallbacks
- **Adaptive Learning**: Learns from conversations and adapts over time
- **Contextual Responses**: Time-aware greetings and situational awareness

### 🔐 Security & Monitoring
- **Sentry Mode**: Facial recognition-enabled security monitoring
- **Motion Detection**: Camera-based motion sensing with fallbacks
- **Network Monitoring**: Intrusion detection and network anomaly alerts
- **Alert System**: Real-time notifications for security events
- **USB Device Monitoring**: Automatic detection and management

### 🧠 AI & Learning
- **Local LLM**: Runs entirely offline using local language models
- **Fallback Responses**: Simple chat system when advanced AI unavailable
- **Self-Training**: Fine-tunes on conversation data
- **Web Exploration**: Autonomous web content discovery and learning
- **Memory Retention**: Persistent conversation history and learned facts
- **No External APIs**: Completely private and secure operation

### 💻 Interface & Control
- **Responsive Web UI**: Beautiful construction-themed interface
- **Touch-Optimized**: Large buttons and intuitive navigation for Pi touchscreen
- **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-based live status updates
- **Mobile Compatible**: Works on tablets and phones
- **System Monitoring**: Real-time hardware and performance metrics

## 🛠️ Hardware Requirements

- **Raspberry Pi 4** (4GB or 8GB recommended)
- **MicroSD Card** (32GB+ recommended, Class 10 or better)
- **Optional Hardware:**
  - Official Raspberry Pi Touchscreen (7-inch)
  - USB Microphone for voice input
  - USB Camera (recommended) for facial recognition
  - Bluetooth speaker or 3.5mm audio output
  - USB devices for expansion

## 📦 Software Stack

| Component | Technology | Purpose |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| **Core** | Python 3.8+ | Main application logic with fallbacks |
| **Web Framework** | Flask + SocketIO | Touchscreen and web interface |
| **AI/ML** | PyTorch, Transformers (optional) | Local language model with fallbacks |
| **Vision** | OpenCV, PIL (optional) | Camera and facial recognition |
| **Audio** | PyAudio, pyttsx3 (optional) | Voice processing with text fallbacks |
| **System** | systemd, psutil | Service management and monitoring |
| **Hardware** | USB device management | USB camera and hardware support |

## 🚀 Quick Start

### 1. Smart Installation

**Option A: Interactive Setup (Recommended)**
```bash
# Clone and setup
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/bro_ai
cd bro_ai
chmod +x install.sh
python3 setup.py  # Interactive setup with feature selection
```

**Option B: Quick Modes**
```bash
# Minimal (web interface only, fastest)
python3 setup.py minimal

# Full features (if you have all hardware)
python3 setup.py full

# Test installation
python3 setup.py test
```

### 2. Running Bro_AI

**Optimized Runner (Recommended):**
```bash
# Web mode with touch interface
python3 run_optimized.py web

# Console mode only
python3 run_optimized.py console

# Test all systems
python3 run_optimized.py test

# Check what features are available
python3 run_optimized.py check
```

**Traditional Method:**
```bash
python3 main.py  # Original implementation
python3 run.py   # Alternative runner
```

### 3. Service Installation

```bash
# Install auto-start service
python3 run_optimized.py install

# Manual service management
sudo systemctl start bro-ai-optimized
sudo systemctl enable bro-ai-optimized  # Auto-start on boot
sudo systemctl status bro-ai-optimized  # Check status
```

